ders-florida-05.jpg\" aria-label=\"Open photo: White aluminum pool screen enclosure protecting pool and patio, installed by Florida pool enclosure contractors.\"><img src=\"/images/images/pool-screen-5/pool-screen-enclosure-builders-florida-05.jpg\" alt=\"White aluminum pool screen enclosure protecting pool and patio, installed by Florida pool enclosure contractors.\" width=\"1250\" height=\"698\" sizes=\"(min-width: 768px) 25vw, 50vw\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"mm-celda\" data-mm-foto=\"/images/images/pool-screen-4/pool-screen-enclosure-builders-florida-04.jpg\" aria-label=\"Open photo: High-end pool cage enclosure with spa and lounge area built by experienced pool screen installers in Florida.\"><img src=\"/images/images/pool-screen-4/pool-screen-enclosure-builders-florida-04.jpg\" alt=\"High-end pool cage enclosure with spa and lounge area built by experienced pool screen installers in Florida.\" width=\"1250\" height=\"698\" sizes=\"(min-width: 768px) 25vw, 50vw\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></button></div><div class=\"mm-mosaico-resto\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"mm-celda mm-celda--resto\" data-mm-foto=\"/images/images/pool-screen-3/pool-screen-enclosure-builders-florida-03.jpg\" aria-label=\"Open photo: Modern pool screen enclosure overlooking lake views, designed and installed by pool enclosure contractors in Florida.\"><img src=\"/images/images/pool-screen-3/pool-screen-enclosure-builders-florida-03.jpg\" alt=\"Modern pool screen enclosure overlooking lake views, designed and installed by pool enclosure contractors in Florida.\" width=\"1250\" height=\"698\" sizes=\"(min-width: 768px) 25vw, 50vw\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"mm-celda mm-celda--resto\" data-mm-foto=\"/images/images/pool-screen-2/pool-screen-enclosure-builders-florida-02.jpg\" aria-label=\"Open photo: Custom pool screen enclosure with outdoor kitchen and seating installed by licensed Florida pool enclosure builders.\"><img src=\"/images/images/pool-screen-2/pool-screen-enclosure-builders-florida-02.jpg\" alt=\"Custom pool screen enclosure with outdoor kitchen and seating installed by licensed Florida pool enclosure builders.\" width=\"1250\" height=\"698\" sizes=\"(min-width: 768px) 25vw, 50vw\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></button></div></div></section><section class=\"mm-proc mm-proc--sin\"><div class=\"mm-sec-cab\"><h2 class=\"mm-h2\">Our Pool Enclosure Build <span class=\"mm-rot\">Process</span></h2><div class=\"mm-sec-lado\"><p class=\"mm-p\">Our licensed contractors design, engineer, and install pool screen enclosures engineered to meet Florida wind codes, safety standards, and all building reg</p><div class=\"mm-sec-acc\"><a class=\"mm-btn mm-btn--linea\" href=\"#estimate\">Get a Free Estimate</a></div></div></div><div class=\"mm-proc-cuerpo\"><ol class=\"mm-pasos\"><li class=\"mm-paso\"><span class=\"mm-paso-n\">1</span><h3 class=\"mm-paso-t\">Screen Type &amp; Configuration Assessment</h3><p>Evaluation of standard aluminum screen enclosure vs. hybrid options. Assessment of pool perimeter dimensions, existing deck configuration, and regulatory requirements for screen material and spacing.</p></li><li class=\"mm-paso\"><span class=\"mm-paso-n\">2</span><h3 class=\"mm-paso-t\">Enclosure Design &amp; Material Selection</h3><p>Design of custom enclosure layout with aluminum framing, screen material selection, roof integration (if applicable), and aesthetic coordination with home architecture. 3D renderings provided.</p></li><li class=\"mm-paso\"><span class=\"mm-paso-n\">3</span><h3 class=\"mm-paso-t\">Permits &amp; Code Compliance</h3><p>Permit acquisition for screen enclosure installation, verification of setback compliance, and ARB approvals if required. Confirmation of screen material specifications per local codes.</p></li><li class=\"mm-paso\"><span class=\"mm-paso-n\">4</span><h3 class=\"mm-paso-t\">Installation &amp; Final Inspection</h3><p>Professional installation of aluminum framing, screen material attachment, hardware installation, and final inspections. Full operational demonstration of any doors or access points.</p></li></ol></div></section><section class=\"mm-que\"><div class=\"mm-sec-cab\"><div class=\"mm-sec-tit\"><p class=\"mm-etiqueta\">What do we do!</p><h2 class=\"mm-h2\">Custom Pool Screen Enclosures &amp; Cage Design Services</h2></div><div class=\"mm-sec-lado\"><p class=\"mm-p\">We build pool screen enclosures in North &amp; South Florida, protecting pools from debris, insects, and harsh sun exposure.</p><div class=\"mm-sec-acc\"><a class=\"mm-btn mm-btn--linea\" href=\"#estimate\">Get a Free Estimate</a></div></div></div><div class=\"mm-que-cuerpo\"><div class=\"mm-que-col\"><ol class=\"mm-grupos\"><li class=\"mm-grupo\"><h3 class=\"mm-grupo-t\">Cage Framing &amp; Roof Profiles</h3><p class=\"mm-grupo-p\">We frame pool cages from extruded aluminum sized to the deck, the roofline, and the setbacks on the lot. Mansard, gable, and hip screen roofs shed water differently, so we pick the profile that suits the house and keeps the clear span within what the framing carries.</p><dl class=\"mm-grupo-dl\"><div class=\"mm-grupo-i\"><dt>Custom Pool Cage Builders</dt><dd>Licensed contractors design and construct pool screen enclosures that blend with residential architecture</dd></div></dl></li><li class=\"mm-grupo mm-grupo--activo\"><h3 class=\"mm-grupo-t\">Lanais, Patios, Screen Rooms</h3><p class=\"mm-grupo-p\">Screening a lanai or converting an open patio adds usable square footage without adding walls. We tie new framing into the existing columns and slab, add kickplates where foot traffic lands, and hang self-closing, self-latching doors so the enclosure holds up as a pool barrier.</p><dl class=\"mm-grupo-dl\"><div class=\"mm-grupo-i\"><dt>Lanai &amp; Patio Enclosure Installation</dt><dd>Installers expand living space by screening patios and lanais, creating bug‑free comfort.</dd></div><div class=\"mm-grupo-i\"><dt>Patio Screen Room Conversion</dt><dd>Contractors convert patios into enclosed screen rooms, creating multi‑use outdoor spaces.</dd></div></dl></li><li class=\"mm-grupo\"><h3 class=\"mm-grupo-t\">Wind Load, Engineering, Permits</h3><p class=\"mm-grupo-p\">Every cage is engineered to the design wind speed the Florida Building Code assigns its address, rising inside Broward's High-Velocity Hurricane Zone and easing farther north. Heavier uprights, tighter beam spacing, and larger concrete anchors follow from that, with sealed drawings for the permit file.</p><dl class=\"mm-grupo-dl\"><div class=\"mm-grupo-i\"><dt>High‑Wind Enclosure Installation</dt><dd>Builders install heavy‑duty screen enclosures engineered for hurricane resistance and safety.</dd></div><div class=\"mm-grupo-i\"><dt>Permit &amp; Engineering Management</dt><dd>Professionals handle permits and engineering for pool cage installations and renovations.</dd></div></dl></li><li class=\"mm-grupo\"><h3 class=\"mm-grupo-t\">Rescreening, Repairs &amp; Remodels</h3><p class=\"mm-grupo-p\">Florida sun and salt air break down screen mesh and fasteners long before the aluminum frame gives out. We rescreen whole cages in 18/14 or no-see-um mesh, swap corroded screws and torn panels, rehang sagging doors, and rebuild dated frames with new uprights and color.</p><dl class=\"mm-grupo-dl\"><div class=\"mm-grupo-i\"><dt>Rescreening &amp; Mesh Replacement</dt><dd>South Florida crews rescreen entire pool enclosures to restore like‑new appearance.</dd></div><div class=\"mm-grupo-i\"><dt>Screen Enclosure Repair Services</dt><dd>Contractors repair damaged panels, fasteners, and doors on existing enclosures for Florida homeowners.</dd></div><div class=\"mm-grupo-i\"><dt>Pool Enclosure Remodeling</dt><dd>Renovation specialists update existing screen enclosures with new framing, doors, and finishes.</dd></div></dl></li></ol><div class=\"mm-datos mm-datos--tel\"><a class=\"mm-dato\" href=\"tel:+13527403361\"><span class=\"mm-dato-rot\">North Florida</span><span class=\"mm-dato-val\">+1 (352) 740-3361</span></a><a class=\"mm-dato\" href=\"tel:+19549137112\"><span class=\"mm-dato-rot\">South Florida</span><span class=\"mm-dato-val\">+1 (954) 913-7112</span></a></div></div><figure class=\"mm-lam-medio mm-que-medio\"><img class=\"mm-lam-foto\" sizes=\"(min-width: 992px) 42vw, 100vw\" src=\"/images/images/pool-screen-9/pool-screen-enclosure-builders-florida-09.jpg\" alt=\"Inside a tall pool cage with loungers and a lake view\" width=\"1250\" height=\"698\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><div class=\"mm-lam-pie\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-n=\"02 / 04\" data-t=\"Lanais, Patios, Screen Rooms\"></div></figure></div></section>";
const T4 = "<section class=\"mm-faq mm-faq--sin\"><div class=\"mm-sec-cab\"><h2 class=\"mm-h2\">Pool Enclosure <span class=\"mm-rot\">FAQs</span></h2><div class=\"mm-sec-lado\"><p class=\"mm-p\">Have questions about pool screen enclosure installation in Florida? Our licensed contractors answer the most common questions from Florida homeowners.</p></div></div><div class=\"mm-faq-cuerpo\"><div class=\"mm-faq-lista\"><details class=\"mm-faq-item\"><summary><h3>Do pool enclosures help protect children and pets?</h3><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"mm-faq-r\"><p>Yes. A permitted pool screen enclosure meets Florida Building Code Chapter 45 barrier requirements, limiting unsupervised access to the pool area. Rob and Val manage the full permit and inspection process — ensuring your enclosure is structurally sound, code-compliant, and approved by the county before final delivery.</p></div></details><details class=\"mm-faq-item\"><summary><h3>How do pool enclosures reduce maintenance?</h3><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"mm-faq-r\"><p>Pool screen enclosures block leaves, insects, airborne debris, and direct UV exposure. Homeowners report significantly less time spent skimming and vacuuming, reduced chemical use, and extended pump and filter life — lowering annual maintenance costs and protecting the long-term condition of your pool system.</p></div></details><details class=\"mm-faq-item\"><summary><h3>Do pool enclosures allow sunlight and natural airflow?</h3><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"mm-faq-r\"><p>Yes. Pool screen enclosures are designed to allow abundant natural light and consistent airflow while filtering UV rays and blocking insects. The fine mesh materials reduce direct solar heat gain, keeping the enclosed area more comfortable during Florida's intense summer months without sacrificing visibility or ventilation.</p></div></details><details class=\"mm-faq-item\"><summary><h3>Are pool enclosures built to Florida hurricane standards?</h3><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"mm-faq-r\"><p>Yes. All pool screen enclosures we install use powder-coated aluminum framing and reinforced mesh engineered to meet Florida's wind-load building codes, including HVHZ requirements in South Florida. Each structure is fully permitted and inspected, ensuring compliance with current ASCE 7-22 structural standards.</p></div></details><details class=\"mm-faq-item\"><summary><h3>Do pool enclosures increase home value in Florida?</h3><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"mm-faq-r\"><p>Yes. A professionally designed pool screen enclosure by Mr. and Mrs. Outdoor Living enhances your backyard visual appeal, extends the usable season, and is recognized by real estate professionals as a desirable feature. In Florida competitive housing market, a permitted, structurally sound enclosure adds measurable value to your property.</p></div></details></div><div class=\"mm-faq-lado\"><div class=\"mm-faq-accion\"><a class=\"mm-btn\" href=\